NAME
       ioctl - device-specific control

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/ioctl.h>

       int ioctl(int fd, unsigned long request, void *arg);

DESCRIPTION
       Performs a device-specific operation on FD.

TERMINAL REQUESTS
       TIOCGWINSZ (0x5413)
              Read the window size into a struct winsize. Full-screen
              programs use it to lay out the display, and the console
              updates it when the font changes.

       TIOCSNONBLOCK (0x5481)
              Take an int; non-zero puts the terminal into non-blocking
              mode for the calling process, so read returns EAGAIN
              rather than waiting. Pass zero to restore blocking.

              This is the mechanism to use for non-blocking terminal
              input: the c_cc VMIN and VTIME fields of termios are
              stored but not honoured, so setting VMIN to 0 does not
              make read return early. poll(2) is the other option and
              is easier when escape sequences must be decoded.

RETURN VALUE
       0 or a request-specific value on success, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF    fd is not open
       ENOTTY   the request does not apply to this file
       EFAULT   arg points outside the address space

SEE ALSO
       poll(2), read(2), termios(3)
